{
  "\nAnalyze the following roleplay segment and create a compact, retrieval-oriented memory entry.\n\nLANGUAGE:\n- Infer the roleplay language from the narrative prose and dialogue, not from character names, metadata labels, JSON property names, or isolated foreign phrases.\n- Write every memory paragraph and every keyword in that same roleplay language.\n- Preserve proper names and established terms exactly. Do not translate or transliterate them.\n\n{{time_contract}}\n\nCONTENT:\n- Produce 3-8 self-contained paragraphs, each covering one distinct meaningful beat.\n- Keep each paragraph to 2-5 concise sentences and under 650 characters.\n- State each fact once only. Do not repeat the same event under separate categories such as story beat, interaction, detail, or outcome.\n- Prioritize durable continuity: decisions, revelations, relationship changes, promises, plans, unresolved threads, important objects, locations, and resulting state.\n- Include a concrete descriptive detail only when it will help distinguish or retrieve the beat later.\n- Exclude casual OOC conversation. Include OOC only when it establishes canonical backstory, a story rule, a formatting requirement, or a scene-setting directive; integrate that fact once into the relevant paragraph.\n- Describe chronology or elapsed time only when narratively important. Never invent a date, day counter, or clock time.\n- Use past tense and third person. Do not add headings, section labels, bullet lists, commentary, or a separate outcome recap inside paragraph text.\n\nKEYWORDS:\n- Give every paragraph 3-7 concrete, scene-specific retrieval keys.\n- Prefer locations, specific objects, organizations, distinctive phrases, revelations, plans, and unique actions.\n- Do not use abstract themes, generic emotions, generic verbs, or a character name by itself.\n- A key may appear on multiple paragraphs only when it genuinely retrieves each of them.\n\nReturn JSON only, without a markdown fence, in this exact shape:\n{\"paragraphs\":[{\"text\":\"one self-contained memory paragraph\",\"keys\":[\"keywords specific to this paragraph\"]}]}\n\nKeep the JSON property names exactly as shown. Do not add any other properties.\n\n{{history}}": "\n分析以下角色扮演片段，生成紧凑、便于检索的记忆条目。\n\n语言：\n- 根据叙述和对话判断角色扮演使用的语言，不要依据角色名、元数据标签、JSON 属性名或零散外语判断。\n- 所有记忆段落和关键词均使用该语言。\n- 专有名称及已确立的术语保持原样，不要翻译或音译。\n\n{{time_contract}}\n\n内容：\n- 输出 3～8 个独立段落，每段概述一个有意义的剧情要点。\n- 每段 2～5 个简洁句子，少于 650 个字符。\n- 每个事实只记录一次，不要把同一事件以剧情、互动、细节、结果等不同类别重复记录。\n- 优先保留影响后续连续性的信息：决定、揭示、关系变化、承诺、计划、未解线索、重要物品、地点和结果状态。\n- 只有有助于区分或检索此要点的具体描写才应保留。\n- 排除日常戏外（OOC）交流。若戏外内容确立了正式背景、故事规则、格式要求或场景指令，则将该事实融入对应段落，且只记录一次。\n- 仅在叙事上重要时描述先后顺序或经过的时间。不得编造日期、天数或具体时刻。\n- 使用过去时态和第三人称。段落正文不加标题、分类标签、项目符号、评论或单独的结果回顾。\n\n关键词：\n- 每段提供 3～7 个具体、与该场景相关的检索关键词。\n- 优先使用地点、具体物品、组织、独特短语、揭示的信息、计划和独特行为。\n- 不使用抽象主题、笼统情绪、泛化动词，也不单独使用角色名。\n- 只有某个关键词确实有助于检索多个段落时，才可重复使用。\n\n仅返回 JSON，不加 Markdown 代码围栏，严格使用此结构：\n{\"paragraphs\":[{\"text\":\"一个内容独立的记忆段落\",\"keys\":[\"此段专属的关键词\"]}]}\n\nJSON 属性名必须与示例完全一致，不得添加其他属性。\n\n{{history}}",
  "TIME:\n- This is an ordinary chat transcript without a Studio-computed clock.\n- Do not infer, calculate, or invent a date, day counter, clock time, duration, or timeline range.\n- Do not put time metadata in paragraph text or JSON. The application owns the entry header.": "时间：\n- 这是普通聊天记录，没有 Studio 计算出的时钟。\n- 不得推断、计算或编造日期、天数、时刻、时长或时间范围。\n- 不在段落正文或 JSON 中添加时间元数据，条目标题由应用管理。",
  "TIME — STUDIO LEDGER:\n- The transcript begins with AUTHORITATIVE_LEDGER_RANGE computed by Studio Ledger. It is source metadata, not dialogue.\n- Preserve that range exactly as supplied. Do not shorten, translate, normalize, recalculate, or replace any part of it.\n- Do not put the range in paragraph text or JSON. The application attaches it to the saved entry header.": "时间 — STUDIO LEDGER：\n- 聊天记录开头的 AUTHORITATIVE_LEDGER_RANGE 由 Studio Ledger 计算，是来源元数据，不属于对话。\n- 完整保留提供的范围，不得缩短、翻译、规范化、重新计算或替换其中任何部分。\n- 不在段落正文或 JSON 中填写该范围，应用会将其附加到保存条目的标题。",
  "\nAnalyze the following roleplay segment and create a concise memory entry.\nPreserve the original language. Do not translate. Exclude all [OOC] conversation.\n\nWrite a compact 3-5 sentence narrative summary in past tense, third person.\nFocus on:\n- What happened (main events and decisions)\n- Key character interactions or developments\n- Important outcome or state change\n\nFor keywords: provide 10-20 concrete, scene-specific keywords:\n- Locations, objects, proper nouns, unique actions\n- NOT abstract themes, emotions, or character names\n\nReturn plain text in this exact format:\nMemory: <3-5 sentence concise narrative summary>\nKeys: <10-20 comma-separated concrete keywords>\n\n{{history}}": "\n分析以下角色扮演片段，生成简洁的记忆条目。\n保留原始语言，不要翻译。排除所有 [OOC] 戏外交流。\n\n使用过去时态、第三人称，撰写 3～5 句紧凑的叙述摘要，重点保留：\n- 发生的主要事件和决定；\n- 重要角色互动及发展；\n- 关键结果或状态变化。\n\n提供 10～20 个具体、与该场景相关的关键词：\n- 地点、物品、专有名词、独特行为；\n- 不使用抽象主题、情绪或角色名。\n\n仅返回纯文本，严格使用以下格式，保留 Memory 和 Keys 标签：\nMemory: <3～5 句简洁叙述摘要>\nKeys: <10～20 个以逗号分隔的具体关键词>\n\n{{history}}",
  "\nAnalyze the following roleplay segment and create a structured memory entry.\nPreserve the original language. Exclude all [OOC] conversation.\n\nUse this markdown structure (skip sections if not applicable):\n**Timeline**: Day/time this scene covers\n**Story Beats**: Important plot events and developments\n**Key Interactions**: Significant character exchanges and relationship shifts\n**Notable Details**: Important objects, settings, revelations, quotes\n**Outcome**: Results, emotional states, consequences\n\nWrite in past tense, third person. Be comprehensive but avoid verbatim repetition.\n\nFor keywords: generate 15-25 concrete scene-specific tags:\n- Proper nouns, locations, specific objects, unique actions\n- NOT abstract concepts, emotions, or character names\n\nReturn plain text in this exact format:\nMemory: <structured markdown summary following the template above>\nKeys: <15-25 comma-separated concrete keywords>\n\n{{history}}": "\n分析以下角色扮演片段，生成结构化记忆条目。\n保留原始语言，排除所有 [OOC] 戏外交流。\n\n使用以下 Markdown 结构，不适用的部分省略：\n**Timeline**：此场景覆盖的日期或时间\n**Story Beats**：重要剧情事件和发展\n**Key Interactions**：重要角色交流和关系变化\n**Notable Details**：重要物品、环境、揭示的信息和引语\n**Outcome**：结果、情绪状态及后果\n\n使用过去时态和第三人称。信息应全面，但避免逐字重复。\n\n提供 15～25 个具体、与该场景相关的关键词：\n- 专有名词、地点、具体物品、独特行为；\n- 不使用抽象概念、情绪或角色名。\n\n仅返回纯文本，严格使用以下格式，保留 Memory 和 Keys 标签：\nMemory: <依照上述模板撰写的结构化 Markdown 摘要>\nKeys: <15～25 个以逗号分隔的具体关键词>\n\n{{history}}",
  "\nCreate a minimal memory entry from the following roleplay segment.\nPreserve the original language. Exclude [OOC] conversation.\n\nWrite 1-2 sentences capturing only the most important factual development.\nFocus on durable outcomes: status changes, revealed facts, decisions, or relationship shifts.\n\nFor keywords: provide 5-10 most relevant concrete keywords (locations, objects, proper nouns).\nDo not use abstract themes or character names.\n\nReturn plain text in this exact format:\nMemory: <1-2 sentence factual summary>\nKeys: <5-10 comma-separated concrete keywords>\n\n{{history}}": "\n从以下角色扮演片段生成极简记忆条目。\n保留原始语言，排除 [OOC] 戏外交流。\n\n仅用 1～2 句记录最重要的事实发展。\n重点保留持续有效的结果：状态变化、已揭示的事实、决定或关系转变。\n\n提供 5～10 个最相关的具体关键词（地点、物品、专有名词）。\n不使用抽象主题或角色名。\n\n仅返回纯文本，严格使用以下格式，保留 Memory 和 Keys 标签：\nMemory: <1～2 句事实摘要>\nKeys: <5～10 个以逗号分隔的具体关键词>\n\n{{history}}",
  "\nWrite a running state of this roleplay, in the language the roleplay is written in.\n\nCover, each in its own short paragraph and only when the conversation gives you something to say:\n- Where the scene stands right now: place, time of day, who is present.\n- What has happened that still matters, in the order it happened.\n- What each character wants, believes, and is hiding.\n- Open threads: promises made, questions unanswered, dangers not yet resolved.\n\nKeep proper names and established terms exactly as they appear. State facts plainly; do not invent, and do not comment on the summary itself.\n": "\n使用角色扮演的原始语言，记录当前剧情状态。\n\n仅根据对话中已有的信息，分别用短段落说明：\n- 当前场景：地点、时段、在场角色；\n- 仍影响后续的事件，按发生顺序记录；\n- 各角色想要什么、相信什么、隐瞒什么；\n- 尚未解决的线索：承诺、未解疑问和未消除的危险。\n\n专有名称及已确立的术语保持原样。直接陈述事实，不得编造，也不评论摘要本身。\n",
  "\nExtract what is established in this roleplay as a flat list of facts, in the language the roleplay is written in.\n\n- One fact per line, starting with \"- \".\n- Each line stands on its own and names who or what it is about.\n- Record only what the conversation establishes: events, relationships, decisions, injuries, possessions, places, promises.\n- Keep proper names and established terms exactly as they appear.\n- No preamble, no closing remark, no speculation.\n": "\n使用角色扮演的原始语言，将已确立的信息提取为平铺的事实清单。\n\n- 每行一项事实，以 \"- \" 开头。\n- 每行应独立完整，并写明涉及的人或事物。\n- 仅记录对话已经确立的内容：事件、关系、决定、伤势、物品归属、地点和承诺。\n- 专有名称及已确立的术语保持原样。\n- 不加开场白、结语或推测。\n",
  "\nSummarize this roleplay in two or three sentences, in the language the roleplay is written in: where the story stands, and the one or two things that matter most for what happens next. Keep proper names exactly as they appear. No preamble.\n": "\n使用角色扮演的原始语言，以两三句话概述当前剧情状态，以及对接下来发展最重要的一两件事。专有名称保持原样，不加开场白。\n",
  "\nYou are given consecutive parts of the summary of one roleplay, oldest first. Merge them into one short summary, in the language they are written in.\n\n- Keep only what the story still needs: where things stand, who is who to each other, what is still open, and what caused the big changes.\n- Retell finished events in a line each, by their outcome.\n- Never present a thread that was resolved as open again.\n- Keep proper names and established terms exactly as written.\n- Add nothing that the parts do not say. No preamble.\n": "\n以下内容是同一段角色扮演的连续摘要，按从旧到新的顺序排列。请使用原始语言，将其合并为一份简短摘要。\n\n- 仅保留后续故事仍需要的信息：当前状态、角色关系、未解线索及重大变化的原因。\n- 已完成的事件各用一句话概述结果。\n- 已解决的线索不得重新描述为未解决。\n- 专有名称及已确立的术语保持原样。\n- 不添加各部分未提及的信息，不加开场白。\n",
  "\nYou are a literary translator for roleplay fiction. Translate the user's message into {{language}}.\n\nTranslate only the text. Do not explain, summarize, censor, annotate or add anything of your own. Preserve the meaning, tone, character voices, dialogue, profanity, names, paragraph breaks, Markdown, HTML tags and their attributes, and any text in square or curly brackets as structure. Translate idioms by meaning. If the text is already in {{language}}, return it unchanged. Reply with the translation only.": "\n你是角色扮演小说的文学译者。请将用户消息翻译为 {{language}}。\n\n只翻译文本，不作解释、总结、审查、注释，也不自行添加内容。保留含义、语气、角色说话风格、对话、粗话、名字、分段、Markdown、HTML 标签及其属性，并保留方括号和花括号内文本的结构。习语按含义翻译。若原文已是 {{language}}，则原样返回。仅回复译文。",
  "\nTranslate the user's message into {{language}}, as faithfully to the original as possible.\n\nTranslate only the text; do not explain or comment. Keep every name, term, number, Markdown and HTML tag exactly as written. Follow the source sentence structure closely, even where a freer rendering would read more naturally. If the text is already in {{language}}, return it unchanged. Reply with the translation only.": "\n请尽可能忠实地将用户消息翻译为 {{language}}。\n\n只翻译文本，不作解释或评论。所有名字、术语、数字、Markdown 和 HTML 标签保持原样。尽量遵循原句结构，即使意译会更自然。若原文已是 {{language}}，则原样返回。仅回复译文。",
  "\nTranslate the user's message into {{language}} the way a native speaker would say it out loud.\n\nTranslate only the text; do not explain or comment. Keep the register, slang and profanity, use natural everyday phrasing, and preserve names, Markdown and HTML tags exactly. If the text is already in {{language}}, return it unchanged. Reply with the translation only.": "\n请将用户消息翻译为 {{language}}，使表达像母语者日常说话一样自然。\n\n只翻译文本，不作解释或评论。保留语体、俚语和粗话，使用自然的日常表达，并原样保留名字、Markdown 和 HTML 标签。若原文已是 {{language}}，则原样返回。仅回复译文。",
  "\nTranslate the user's message into {{language}}. Translate only the text, do not explain, and reply with nothing but the translation.": "\n将用户消息翻译为 {{language}}。只翻译文本，不作解释，回复中只包含译文。"
}
